From bff8f88c6b36d175de50550c2742f8a83ecc058e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 01:51:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] Switch HTTP listener to native Bun.serve
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace @hono/node-server's createAdaptorServer with Bun.serve and
@hono/node-ws's createNodeWebSocket with hono/bun's createBunWebSocket.

Native Bun.serve runs Hono on Bun's uWebSockets path. `req.signal.abort`
fires synchronously from `RequestContext.onAbort` via
`us_socket_context_on_close` (EPOLLRDHUP) — no batching of socket-close
events behind unrelated I/O. WebSocket close events go through the
same path, so per-connection cleanup is reliable across all transports.

Mechanically:
  - `createNodeWebSocket({app})` → `createBunWebSocket()` (hono/bun).
    Same `upgradeWebSocket` shape, existing `PtyRoutes` consumer is
    unaffected.
  - `createAdaptorServer({fetch})` + `server.listen` → `Bun.serve({
    fetch, websocket, port, hostname })`.
  - Pass `server` as 2nd arg to `app.fetch(req, server)` so
    `getBunServer(c)` can locate it for WebSocket upgrades.
  - `server.address().port` → `server.port`.
  - `server.close(cb)` → `server.stop(close ?? false)`.

Drops the @hono/node-server and @hono/node-ws dependencies. The
listener is independently valid as a cleanup; it's also a prerequisite
for the per-client WebSocket presence channel that follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
